  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Piyush Sharma vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 22 April, 2025 Author: Achal Kumar Paliwal Bench: Achal Kumar Paliwal Neutral Citation No. 2025:Mphc-Jbp:18288 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Achal Kumar Paliwal On The 22 nd Of April, 2025 Misc. Criminal Case No. 14893 of 2025 Piyush Sharma Versus The State Of Madhya Pradesh And Others Appearance: Ms. Nupur Dhamija - Deputy Government Advocate for the resp Order",
    "facts": "The applicant is in jail since 26.03.2025 in connection with Crime No. RCT No.8404 of 2024 registered at P.S. Arera Hills, District-Bhopal for the offence punishable under Sections 426, 465, 468 and 471 of the IPC. 3. Prosecution story in brief is that co-accused forged rent agreement dated 16.10.2018 in the name of complainant and thereafter used above forged rent agreement for obtaining the license from Food safety and Controller and Drug Administration and allegation against present applicant is that he signed the aforesaid rent agreement as witness. 4. Learned counsel for the applicant submits that Satish Sharma is main accused and he has been released on bail by this Court vide order dated 29.01.2025 passed in M.Cr.C.No.1355 of 2025 ( Satish Sharma Vs. The State of Madhya Pradesh and Others). After investigation, charge-sheet has been filed.",
    "arguments": "5. Learned Deputy Government Advocate for the State submits that from report of handwriting expert, it is evident that rent agreement dated 16.10.2018 has not been prepared and signed by the complainant. Thus, applicant has prepared a forged document.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. Learned Deputy Government Advocate for the State submits that from report of handwriting expert, it is evident that rent agreement dated 16.10.2018 has not been prepared and signed by the complainant.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Thus, applicant has prepared a forged document.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
